.TH COASTLINE-IMPORT-PAK 1 "2026-11-01" "Coastline @CMAKE_PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coastline-import-pak \- import Top Gear Rally Controller Pak notes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coastline
.RI [ options ]
.B import-pak
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy recognised Top Gear Rally notes from FILE into Coastline's Controller Pak
data.
USA, European, and Japanese releases are accepted.
Unrelated notes and invalid page chains are skipped.
A recognised note replaces a saved note with the same identifier.
.PP
FILE must be a 32 KiB Controller Pak image or a 128 KiB four-pak image.
Only the first pak of a four-pak image is imported.
Global options precede import-pak.
Use \-\-data-dir to select the destination data directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print subcommand usage and exit.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Console Time Attack ghost notes provide recorded controller input.
Import does not convert the recording into pose frames required by the PC race
engine.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
coastline import-pak controller.mpk
coastline \-\-data-dir ./game-data import-pak backup.mpk
.fi
.PP
Export saved notes with the following command.
.nf
coastline export-pak \-\-release usa backup.mpk
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates that the image was processed.
Skipped unrelated or invalid notes do not make an otherwise valid import fail.
A nonzero status indicates invalid arguments, an invalid image, or a write
failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coastline (1),
.BR coastline-import (1)
